NAME
     sed - edit a stream of text

SYNOPSIS
     sed [-n] [-E] [-i] [-e SCRIPT] [-f FILE] [SCRIPT] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     sed reads each line, applies the script to it and prints the result.
     The script is the usual language: addresses (a line number, $, a
     /regexp/, or two of them for a range) in front of commands --
     s///, p, d, a, i, c, y///, n, N, q, =, b, t, labels, and { } for a
     group.

OPTIONS
     -n          print nothing unless the script says to
     -E          extended regular expressions
     -i          edit the files in place
     -e SCRIPT   add SCRIPT to the program
     -f FILE     read the program from FILE

EXAMPLES
     sed -n '/error/p' /var/log/messages
     sed -i 's/tabs/spaces/g' notes.txt

SEE ALSO
     awk(1), grep(1), tr(1)
